WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.160
Nearly four-fifths of the air
around us is nitrogen gas:

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.310
about 78 per cent.

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.950
Living things need nitrogen to build
their proteins and nucleic acids.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.540
A field of crops sits in that
air every hour of every day.

5
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.730
So why do crops so often
run short of nitrogen,

6
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.790
when they are surrounded by it?

7
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.280
In this mission, you'll see why the elements
living things need are recycled through

8
00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:28.090
an ecosystem, again and again.

9
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:32.230
Then you'll see why energy is
different: it passes straight through,

10
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.890
and leaves as heat.

11
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:39.160
Your mission: find out how crops can
lack nitrogen in a world so full of it.
